## 📖 Overview
## 📄 Abstract

Artificial intelligence has become an increasingly important tool in education, changing how students search for and process information. This study compares ChatGPT and traditional search engines in terms of usability, response quality, speed, and trustworthiness.

The research combines a survey of 75 participants, an experimental comparison using five academic questions, and a qualitative analysis of students' opinions. The findings indicate that ChatGPT provides faster and more user-friendly responses, while traditional search engines remain the preferred source for verifying factual information.

The results suggest that the most effective approach is to combine AI-powered tools with traditional search engines to support learning and academic research.

This repository contains my independent research project comparing ChatGPT and traditional search engines for educational information retrieval.

The research investigates how students use artificial intelligence and traditional search engines for academic purposes through a survey, an experimental comparison, and qualitative analysis.


## 🎯 Research Objectives

- Compare ChatGPT and Google Search in educational information retrieval.
- Evaluate response quality and response time.
- Analyze students' preferences and trust.
- Explore the role of AI in modern education.


## 🔬 Methodology

This study consists of three parts:

- 📋 Survey of 75 participants
- 🧪 Experimental comparison using 5 academic questions
- 💬 Qualitative analysis of 15 open-ended responses
  

